  culturalContextData:
  - {fileID: 5638779662687437508}
  - {fileID: 5638779662324042654}
  - {fileID: 5638779663125664309}
  - {fileID: 5638779663233243550}
  questionDescription: {fileID: 5638779662065520565}
  aButton: {fileID: 5638779662284212045}
  bButton: {fileID: 5638779661579442705}
  cButton: {fileID: 5638779663058220302}
  dButton: {fileID: 5638779662592768907}
  scoreText: {fileID: 5638779662558988451}
  outputText: {fileID: 5638779662332016703}
  resultPanel: {fileID: 5638779663181551894}
  quizQuestions:
  - question: "What is the origin of the Cari\xF1osa dance?"
    choices:
    - A) Luzon
    - B) Visayas
    - C) Mindanao
    - D) Panay Island
    correctAnswer: D) Panay Island
  - question: "Which Spanish dances influenced the Cari\xF1osa?"
    choices:
    - A) Flamenco and Salsa
    - B) Bolero and Jarabe Tapatio
    - C) Tango and Rumba
    - D) Fandango and Paso Doble
    correctAnswer: B) Bolero and Jarabe Tapatio
  - question: "What is a common prop used in the Cari\xF1osa?"
    choices:
    - A) Hat
    - B) Fan or handkerchief
    - C) Cane
    - D) Umbrella
    correctAnswer: B) Fan or handkerchief
  - question: "What type of costumes are traditionally worn during the Cari\xF1osa?"
    choices:
    - A) Modern dancewear
    - B) Maria Clara gown and Barong Tagalog
    - C) T-shirt and jeans
    - D) Traditional Japanese kimonos
    correctAnswer: B) Maria Clara gown and Barong Tagalog
  - question: "The Cari\xF1osa dance is associated with which cultural practice?"
    choices:
    - A) Religious ceremonies
    - B) Courtship rituals
    - C) Harvest festivals
    - D) Warrior training
    correctAnswer: B) Courtship rituals
  - question: "What is the order of the Cari\xF1osa figures?"
    choices:
    - A) Figure 1 (Three-step and point), Figure 2 (Touch Step), Figure 3 (3-Step
      Forward and Back to Back), Figure 4 (Hide and Seek with Fan), Figure 5 (Kneeling
      and Fanning), Figure 6 (Hide and Seek w/ Handkerchief), Figure 7 (Flirting
      w/ Handkerchief), Figure 8 (Flirting)
    - B)  Figure 1 (Touch Step), Figure 2 (Three-step and point), Figure 3 (3-Step
      Forward and Back to Back), Figure 4 (Hide and Seek with Fan), Figure 5 (Kneeling
      and Fanning), Figure 6 (Hide and Seek w/ Handkerchief), Figure 7 (Flirting
      w/ Handkerchief), Figure 8 (Flirting)
    - C) Figure 1 (Touch Step), Figure 2 (Three-step and point), Figure 3 (3-Step
      Forward and Back to Back), Figure 4 (Hide and Seek with Fan), Figure 5 (Kneeling
      and Fanning), Figure 6 (Hide and Seek w/ Handkerchief), Figure 7 (Flirting),
      Figure 8 (Flirting w/ Handkerchief)
    - D) Figure 1 (Flirting), Figure 2 (Three-step and point), Figure 3 (3-Step Forward
      and Back to Back), Figure 4 (Hide and Seek with Fan), Figure 5 (Kneeling and
      Fanning), Figure 6 (Hide and Seek w/ Handkerchief), Figure 7 (Touch Step),
      Figure 8 (Flirting w/ Handkerchief)
    correctAnswer: A) Figure 1 (Three-step and point), Figure 2 (Touch Step), Figure
      3 (3-Step Forward and Back to Back), Figure 4 (Hide and Seek with Fan), Figure
      5 (Kneeling and Fanning), Figure 6 (Hide and Seek w/ Handkerchief), Figure
      7 (Flirting w/ Handkerchief), Figure 8 (Flirting)
  - question: "In which historical period did the Cari\xF1osa originate?"
    choices:
    - A) Pre-colonial era
    - B) Spanish colonial period
    - C) American colonial period
    - D) Post-independence era
    correctAnswer: B) Spanish colonial period
  - question: "What type of music is commonly used in the Cari\xF1osa?"
    choices:
    - A) Classical symphony
    - B) Modern pop
    - C) Traditional folk music
    - D) Jazz
    correctAnswer: C) Traditional folk music
  - question: "The Cari\xF1osa dance is characterized by what type of movements?"
    choices:
    - A) Rapid and vigorous
    - B) Slow and graceful
    - C) Sharp and precise
    - D) Athletic and energetic
    correctAnswer: B) Slow and graceful
  - question: "What does the word Cari\xF1osa mean in English?"
    choices:
    - A) The Dancer
    - B) The Lover
    - C) The Friend
    - D) The Leader
    correctAnswer: B) The Lover
  - question: "Which Filipino historical figure is known for documenting the Cari\xF1osa?"
    choices:
    - A) Jose Rizal
    - B) Andres Bonifacio
    - C) Francisca Reyes Aquino
    - D) Emilio Aguinaldo
    correctAnswer: C) Francisca Reyes Aquino
  - question: "What is a primary feature of the Cari\xF1osa dance performance?"
    choices:
    - A) Solo performances
    - B) Pair dancing with flirtatious gestures
    - C) Group choreography with acrobatics
    - D) Silent mime acts
    correctAnswer: B) Pair dancing with flirtatious gestures
  - question: "What does the Cari\xF1osa dance celebrate?"
    choices:
    - A) Historical battles
    - B) Religious ceremonies
    - C) Romance and courtship
    - D) Agricultural harvests
    correctAnswer: C) Romance and courtship
  - question: "Which dance form is the Cari\xF1osa most closely related to?"
    choices:
    - A) Ballet
    - B) Tap Dance
    - C) Spanish Court Dance
    - D) Modern Dance
    correctAnswer: C) Spanish Court Dance
  - question: "What is the role of the fan or handkerchief in the Cari\xF1osa?"
    choices:
    - A) To keep cool
    - B) To accentuate the dance moves and gestures
    - C) To signal the end of the performance
    - "D) To hide the dancers\u2019 faces"
    correctAnswer: B) To accentuate the dance moves and gestures
