    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 1
    m_MinSize: 10
    m_MaxSize: 42
    m_Alignment: 4
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "Traditional Costumes: Performers of Cari\xF1osa traditionally wear elegant
    Maria Clara gowns for women and Barong Tagalog for men. These costumes not only
    reflect Spanish influence but also embody Filipino national pride and identity.\r\n\nCultural
    Significance: Beyond its historical context, Cari\xF1osa is a celebration of
    romance and courtship. Its lively movements and graceful gestures illustrate
    the charm and courtship rituals of traditional Filipino society.\r\n\nExperience
    it in VR: Immerse yourself in the graceful and romantic world of Cari\xF1osa.
    Explore the dance's intricate steps, and traditional costumes in a fully interactive
    and immersive virtual environment. Discover the beauty of Filipino-Spanish cultural
    fusion firsthand!"
